       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose is well above the usual maximum for metformin.\n\n- **Ordered:** 1700 mg three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release in adults. Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day. Single doses are usually 500\u20131000 mg, and no more than 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Risk:** This is about twice the maximum. It raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg PO three times daily with meals**, or another dose\n\nIf 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
